    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "The status is `open` and that is the WRONG WORD, used because the schema's enum offers nothing better. This proposition is a settled theorem; what is open is not the mathematics but whether this repository can say it. The vocabulary conflates the epistemic status OF A PROPOSITION with the evidence status IN THIS LEDGER, and those come apart exactly here -- see the lane diary for the proposed `established-elsewhere` value. What the gap actually is: our IR has terms for values and functions over sorts, and no term for a syntactic object. Godel numbering is not the obstacle -- arithmetic on codes we could do -- the obstacle is that `provable-in-T` would have to be a predicate over our own formulas, and formulas are not in the domain of discourse. Every fact in this batch that says 'this is a metatheorem we cannot state' (F:resolution-rule-sound on completeness, F:exportation on the deduction theorem, F:tseitin-and-gate on general equisatisfiability) is blocked by that same single missing thing: reflection.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
